  "title": "Carol G NDE 22889",
  "date": "December 10, 2012",
  "content": "December 10, 2012, 9:30 am. I went on a work errand. As I walked toward my car there was a family parked beside my car that was backing up. I moved back to give the driver room, as I knew I was in his blind spot. As I approached the end of a parking row, my left foot slipped on ice and my front foot went flying. When I realized I was falling I dropped my purse and tucked my head forward to position myself for a break fall that I had learned as a child in Judo classes. I could not keep my head tucked. I tried to control it as it whipped back. Everything went into slow motion. I could hear the hair swishing back within the slow motion. It was so slow that I thought I could count the number of hairs on my head. Knowing that I couldn't control the fall, I told myself to just relax and go with it. I knew I was no longer in control and just went with the fall. I opened my eyes. It was like seeing for the first time, everything was very bright on this dark, snowy day. The building I had just exited was in total blackness in my left peripheral vision. I could see traffic moving in front of me, as well as on the off ramp. From my right, when I looked down, I saw a body falling. I said aloud, ’that's Carol.’ It came out in a whisper of several voices, both female and male. I rushed to help the falling person when I was suddenly back inside the body. I could feel the pain on the top of my head that already existed and I felt the second hit to the back of the head. I said out loud in single voice, ‘Thank you God for not letting it hit in the same place twice.’",
